  "evidences": [
    {
      "id": "ev_2",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "UnFIN4ished_Business_pwd",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s2"
      },
      "text": "FIN4 is a financially motivated threat actor which has consistently targeted this population.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_4",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "UnFIN4ished_Business_pwd",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s4"
      },
      "text": "In particular, the FIN4 group has shown a particular interest in the healthcare and pharmaceutical industry and appears to have team members who are intimately familiar with that industry.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_6",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "UnFIN4ished_Business_pwd",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s6"
      },
      "text": "These reports document two methods of attack used by the FIN4 group: malicious Microsoft Office documents to obtain credentials, and phishing pages designed to mimic Outlook Web App authentication pages.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_7",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "UnFIN4ished_Business_pwd",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s7"
      },
      "text": "The UpDocX Malware",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_8",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "UnFIN4ished_Business_pwd",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s1"
      },
      "text": "However, in our sample the macro code differs, in that it uses URLDownloadToFile to download an executable named WINWORD32.exe - this can be seen below.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_10",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "UnFIN4ished_Business_pwd",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s1"
      },
      "text": "Due to the command and control filename as shown in the htmlUpload function below, we refer to this malware as UpDocX:",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_11",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "UnFIN4ished_Business_pwd",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s2"
      },
      "text": "UpDocX was written in VB.NET and compiled without any attempts at obfuscating the source code.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_14",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "UnFIN4ished_Business_pwd",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s5"
      },
      "text": "UpDocX has a list of extensive clean-up functions responsible for eliminating evidence of compromise, which indicates a degree of caution often not observed in targeted attacks.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_15",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "UnFIN4ished_Business_pwd",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s6"
      },
      "text": "We believe that one of the authors of UpDocX may be a French speaker, based on naming conventions used in the malware.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_16",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "UnFIN4ished_Business_pwd",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s7"
      },
      "text": "PwC threat intelligence customers can access a more detailed technical analysis of UpDocX, additional indicators associated with FIN4 and our most recent profile of the group, in report reference CTO-TAP-20150518-01A.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_18",
